{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Abram: Go for yourself.</b> This is the meaning of 'Go for yourself' in Old French — while Terah was still in Ur Kasdim. Another interpretation: <b>From your land</b> — from Haran, where you dwell, as it is written above: 'They came as far as Haran and settled there.'" "<b>And from your birthplace.</b> So that you not say, 'I will return to the land of my birthplace, I will return to my father's house, for the sake of my inheritance' — for I will bless you beyond the amount of your inheritance. Rashi commented here, and here you are not worthy of children — this is what our Rabbis said: three things annul the decree: change of place, and calling out the Name, etc." "<b>To the land</b> etc. Because he was of the seed of Shem, to whom the land fell as his portion, as Rashi explained. The Holy One, blessed be He, led him to walk about in it."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:55.736553199Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}